  "notes": "きつい is an i-adjective with a wide range of meanings from physical tightness to emotional harshness.\n\nFORMS:\n- Adverb: きつく\n- Noun form: きつさ\n\nCOMMON USES:\n- {服|ふく}がきつい: clothes are tight\n- {坂|さか}がきつい: the slope is steep/demanding\n- {性格|せいかく}がきつい: personality is harsh\n- {仕事|しごと}がきつい: work is tough/demanding\n- きつい{言|い}い{方|かた}: harsh way of speaking\n- {匂|にお}いがきつい: smell is strong/overpowering\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- きつい vs. {厳|きび}しい: きつい emphasizes difficulty or discomfort; {厳|きび}しい emphasizes strictness or severity",
